===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:bor|frm:methode|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sed-}}
From {{bor|en|frm|methode}}, from {{der|en|la|methodus}}, from {{der|en|grc|μέθοδος}}. {{surf|en|met-|-hod}}. See also [[-ode]] and [[hodo-]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[process]] by which a [[task]] is [[completed]]; a way of doing something (followed by the [[adposition]] [[of]], [[to]] or [[for]] before the purpose of the process).
#: {{ux|en|If one '''method''' doesn't work, you should ask a friend to help you.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=3|passage=He at once secured attention by his informal '''method''', and when presently the coughing of Jarvis {{...}} interrupted the sermon, he altogether captivated his audience with a remark about cough lozenges being cheap and easily procurable.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/william-e-conner-1 William E. Conner]|title=An Acoustic Arms Race|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/an-acoustic-arms-race|volume=101|issue=3|page=206–7|magazine=w:American Scientist|passage=Many insects probably use this strategy, which is a close analogy to crypsis in the visible world—camouflage and other '''methods''' for blending into one’s visual background.|accessdate=2 July 2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130717135348/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/an-acoustic-arms-race|archivedate=17 July 2013}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[systematicity|Systematicity]], [[methodicalness]], [[intentionality]], [[order]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=II|scene=ii|page=261|column=2|passage=Though this be madneſſe, / Yet there is '''Method''' in 't: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=06 Dec 80|volume=8|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=14|title=Mousie Mousie Wildflower (personal advertisement)|text=There's '''method''' in the universe.<br>We're lucky that things aren't worse.}}
# {{lb|en|acting|often "the method"}} A technique for [[acting]] based on the ideas articulated by {{w|Konstantin Stanislavski}} and focusing on authentically experiencing the inner life of the character being portrayed.
#: {{syn|en|method acting}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Kenneth Branagh|title=Beginning|year=1989|publisher=Chatto & Windus|location=London |pageurl=https://archive.org/details/beginning0000bran_q0a2/page/64/mode/1up|page=64|isbn=978-0-7011-3388-7|passage=In this case, the application of the famous '''method''' was a little shaky. To be fair, the director was dealing with a pretty stroppy cast.}}
# {{senseid|en|object-oriented programming}} {{lb|en|object-oriented}} A [[subroutine]] or [[function]] belonging to a [[class]] or [[object]].
#: {{syn|en|member function}}
